# README — Source Data: Multi-Omics Heatmap (Discovery and Validation Cohorts)

## Overview
This file contains the numerical values underlying the multi-omics heatmap figure(s)
showing driver markers across the Discovery and Validation cohorts of the 2000HIV
study (NCT03994835). It accompanies the manuscript "Multi-Omics Clustering
Differentiates the Total and Intact HIV Reservoirs and Related Host Immune
Mechanisms."

## Sheet contents

### Discovery_Data / Validation_Data
Each row corresponds to one marker (feature) selected as a validated driver marker
(i.e., identified as a cluster-defining feature in both the Discovery and Validation
cohorts via MoCluster feature selection).

- **Column 1 (Omic_Layer):** the omics data type the marker belongs to
  (Bulk_transcriptomics, Proteomics, Flowcytometry_abs, Methylation, Ex_Vivo,
  Viral_Reservoir).
- **Column 2 (Marker):** marker/feature name.
- **Remaining columns:** one column per sample, containing the standardized value
  plotted in the heatmap (see "Data processing" below).

### Endotype_Label
Each row corresponds to one sample.

- **Column 1 (Sample_ID):** sample identifier, consistent with sample IDs used as
  column headers in the Discovery_Data and Validation_Data sheets.
- **Column 2 (Cluster_Label):** the immune-reservoir endotype assigned to that
  sample by multi-omics clustering (All Low / All High / Mixed).

## Data processing
Values shown in Discovery_Data and Validation_Data are **standardized** values, not
raw measurements:
- Per-omics-layer standardization was performed using `getStdiz()` (MOVICS package),
  with centering and scaling applied.
- Standardization was performed independently within the Discovery and Validation
  cohorts.

Units of the underlying (pre-standardization) measurements per omics layer:
- Bulk transcriptomics: log2-transformed counts
- Proteomics: NPX (log2)
- Flow cytometry: absolute cell counts (log2)
- DNA methylation: M-values
- Ex-vivo cytokine production: log2-transformed concentrations
- Viral reservoir (HIV-1 DNA): log2-transformed copies

## Raw (pre-standardization) data availability
Raw, unstandardized data for all omics layers are deposited in the Radboud Data
Repository (RDR) and are accessible to reviewers upon request/following the access
instructions provided in the manuscript's Data Availability statement:
- Bulk RNA-seq, DNA methylation, ex-vivo cytokine production:
  https://doi.org/10.34973/p96d-kz55
- Proteomics: https://doi.org/10.34973/qk29-f305
- HIV-1 DNA reservoir data: https://doi.org/10.34973/2bf5-yc03
- Flow cytometry: RDR collection ru.rumc.2000hiv_t0000321a_dsc_002


